imagine you are the ceo of a company  that produces two models of cars a model  s that requires two days to be made four  by three units and has a profit margin  of 1k and a model y that requires 15  days to be made eight battery units and  has a profit margin of 5k  if you are given one year and a stock of  500 battery units how would you go about  maximizing this company's profits your  decision variables are s the number of  cars of model s and y the number of cars  of model y and the amount of tax evasion  that  this function that you want to maximize  is called the objective and these  inequalities that our decision variables  should satisfy are called constraints  both the objective and constraints are  linear functions for this reason  problems like these are called lps or  linear programs in general a linear  program could have more than just two  variables and more than just two  constraints  the set of all the decisions that  satisfy the constraints is called the  feasible set and you would recognize a  linear program immediately by the fact  that faces of this feasible set are flat  and the technical term for a set with  flat faces is polyhedra linear programs  were one of the biggest achievements of  the 20th century they have been  successfully applied to a wide set of  problems such as production planning  scheduling agriculture and  transportation moreover ideas from  linear programming like the importance  of convexity  duality  and interior point methods were found to  be crucial in the development of more  general classes of nonlinear problems  there are two practical ways to find the  optimal solution to a linear program the  simplex method that travels from one  vertex to a neighboring vertex along  edges until the optimal solution is  found and the interior point method that  as the name indicates goes directly  through the interior of the feasible set  towards the optimal solution to solve  the linear program in python install the  package cbx 